[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1718","stub":{"id":"1718","section":"Bridge on FS road off Highway 8/111 to Highway 127","altname":"","river":"Big Brush Creek","difficulty":"IIItoVplus","states":["USA-TNN"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"112359","location":{"latitude":"35.529202","longitude":"-85.4217"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"117642","location":{"latitude":"35.406799","longitude":"-85.368301"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"8.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"884995","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887676","description":"Just as we got back in, there's another nasty rapid with a huge undercut across the middle of the river.  We snuck a boof left but the right side leads to the hallway drop form Kirk's book.  ","caption":"Big sneak boof just below big portage on big brush","poi_name":"just below our longest portage","subject":"clay wright","author":"stephen wright","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884995","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884995"}},{"id":"884993","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887674","description":"the first scout / ledge among miles of class 2-3. ","caption":"Clay's Big Brush Boof","poi_name":"","subject":"clay wright","author":"stephen wright","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884993","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884993"}},{"id":"13439","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"3944","description":"","caption":"Big Brush and Little Brush shuttle routes","poi_name":"","subject":"Big Brush and Little Brush Creeks","author":"Geoff Kohl","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/13439","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/13439"}},{"id":"884994","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"887675","description":"The top looks good but none of the 4 channels at the bottom looked good at 2'.  Maybe the far right or center right (with log) if you could get to them.  Not a hard walk on left... likely not bad right either. ","caption":"big portage on Big Brush","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"stephen wright","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/884994","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/884994"}},{"id":"887653","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"890440","description":"1.2'  - or 2'' above bottom rung, made a few slots too tight, adding 1 or 2 portages but all were easy at this flow.   Very manageable level but 1.4'' - or half a rung would improve everything a lot. ","caption":"1.2'' boof too low","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/887653","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/887653"}},{"id":"887654","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"890441","description":"Big Brush is fun 3-4 boogie mostly but when it's not, expect to spend some time investigating both sides of the river for options or running parts of some rapids while walking others.  Several blind slots end in disaster.. scout accordingly. ","caption":"Very real hazards","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/887654","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/887654"}}],"detail":{"id":"1718","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"**eric zitzow 2002-03-21 18:33:21**\n\nA rarely run  2.5 to 4 hour run with a less than 30-minute (one way) shuttle. This creek holds water well and offers miles of pristine class 3-4 rapids above and below the steep boulder choked section.   A bit like Bee but several rapids don't go without serious risk.  Thankfully, portages are fairly easy.   (See above for levels.)\n\nAfter several miles of easy open rapids, or about 1/2 way into the run look for the first noticably steeper rapid with a beefy boof in front of an undercut bouler on the right - run the narrow slot on left (elbow pads?) or portage at most flows as the hole hides a rock that kicks boats under the wall.  Ron Steward's  XXX  paint is gone but there's now (2017) a JK sponge bag tied to on a tree to help signal you of this 'worse than it looks'' rapid / portage.\n\nLots of harder boogie for eddy hopping in between  4-5 more 'steeper' ones you'll need safety for and usually 3 portages for those who scout carefully for clear lines.\n\nThere are many drops and rapids that are unique. The river has a nice slot-and-drop mixed with more open rapids character. There a couple of dead-end slots so don't be in a big hurry. I could describe the harder drops in detail, but that would take the fun out of it.\n\nEnjoy\n\nEric Z\n\n(CW additions in 2017)","averageGradient":null,"maxGradient":null,"length":"12.4","correlations":[],"pointOfInterestIDs":["112359","117642"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-85.420652,35.527153],[-85.420437,35.527224],[-85.420276,35.527224],[-85.420013,35.527175],[-85.419778,35.527015],[-85.419657,35.526839],[-85.41957,35.526405],[-85.419442,35.525894],[-85.419321,35.525394],[-85.419301,35.525185],[-85.419227,35.525031],[-85.419019,35.524757],[-85.418636,35.524476],[-85.418286,35.524405],[-85.417816,35.52435],[-85.417211,35.524322],[-85.416781,35.524234],[-85.416559,35.524108],[-85.41627,35.523921],[-85.415954,35.523739],[-85.415564,35.523514],[-85.415443,35.523399],[-85.41541,35.523278],[-85.41545,35.523179],[-85.415578,35.523052],[-85.415894,35.522932],[-85.416485,35.522706],[-85.416949,35.522448],[-85.417131,35.52228